  "edits": "First bar requests explicit50 on the absent beat, removes the derived mark, changes zero to derived, and changes one reused 12345 occurrence to4000. Other occurrence remains12345.",
  "acceptance": [
    "Absent, derived and authored timer states are distinct in the public model and raw final consumer for ordinary beats.",
    "Explicit zero/nonzero and exact integer endpoints retain their beat addresses; mutable repeated occurrences are independent.",
    "Public edits retain the supported distinction and invalid values have exact diagnostics. Grace-beat timer conversion remains an explicit source limitation; the broad any-beat retention criterion is not marked complete."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No playback timer is calculated. AlphaTab MIDI generation can subsequently overwrite values; this receipt observes the completed importer before MIDI generation.",
    "Public milliseconds must be in 0..9007199254740991. This evidenced safe-integer limit is a library contract, not a universal GPIF numeric limit.",
    "Source empty and -1 mean requested derived time. Other negative, fractional, overflowing or invalid text receives GPIF.Beat.Timer.InvalidValue; permissive import retains a derived request and strict import rejects it.",
    "Grace-beat Timer99 survives the pinned source importer but has no destination in GraceEffect. GPIF.Beat.Timer.GraceUnsupported diagnoses it and strict source import rejects it. Permissive import drops the timer while retaining the grace note; the exported artifact exposes this residual under #108."
  ],
  "tests": [
    "TestBeatTimerPublicStates",
    "TestConformanceBeatTimer",
    "TestBeatTimerInvalidSource",
    "TestAlphaTabBeatTimer",
    "TestBeatTimerGraceSourceLimit"
  ],
